  "source_magnitude_definition": "Actual adopted r magnitude: NSC r median where available, otherwise SDSS r. These source-count bins are not the independent spectroscopic r bins of the QSO comparisons; neither measures a photometric-parent completeness.",
  "readout_implementation_sha256": "4f3668536ba117daed456e3db04089a507328ec4ea210c1930ca6a94e2625a4b",
  "denominator_notes": "Origin counts and funnel stages are before common-epoch transfer/global identity exclusions. Component detection applications count normalized core positions, not globally unique measurements; do not pool across disconnected component applications. Anchors enter the r funnel after morphology and core selection, and stage counters overlap; they are not an all-photometric parent. No new selection, fit, DCR or error rescaling. Native support, spherical association and weighting changed together in the full update; these receipt counts do not causally isolate their source gains. The fixed v2.1 controlled experiments and v2.2 fixed-identity comparisons supply the separate tests. Source-worker elapsed is summed worker walltime, not CPU or allocation billing. Independent/reference SEs are conditional mas/yr, not absolute systematic uncertainties. Quality flags overlap and do not certify stellar identity or spatial zero.",
